<title>GERMANY: German savings banks set up subsidiary in Dublin.</title>
<headline>German savings banks set up subsidiary in Dublin.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deka, the fund management unit of the German savings bank organisation, said on Monday it planned to set up a subsidiary in Dublin, Ireland, to launch global investment funds.</p>
<p>Deka, which has 110 billion marks of funds under management, said it would find it increasingly difficult to satisfy the demands of savings bank clients unless it expands internationally.</p>
<p>The group already has subsidiaries in Luxembourg and Zurich, DekaBank GmbH, which acts as management holding company for the group, said in a statement.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
